# `docs/adr/index.md` and `.claude/rules/adr-pointers.md` are generated from the front matter of the
# records in `docs/adr/`. Two branches that each add a record always conflict in them, and the
# resolution is never a merge — it is `make adr-index`. This driver does exactly that, so the
# conflict resolves itself.
#
# A driver has to be registered locally before git will use it: `make setup-git`, which `make
# install` runs. Without it git falls back to the ordinary text merge and you get the conflict you
# would have got anyway, so a clone that skips the setup is no worse off than before.
docs/adr/index.md            merge=adr-generated
.claude/rules/adr-pointers.md merge=adr-generated
